.TH IRON86 1 "2026-09-04" "iron86 0.13" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
iron86 \- chip-level 8086 IBM PC (no DOS)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iron86
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fIfile.com\fR]
.P
.B iron86
.BI \-\-bios " BIOS.BIN"
[\fB\-\-floppy\-a\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-floppy\-b\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-keys\fR \fISTRING\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B iron86
is a C++23 8086 + IBM PC chip set (PPI, PIT, PIC, DMA, FDC, two 6845s).
It does not implement DOS; FloppyOS or a BIOS INT 19 boot provides that.
.P
.B tdx \-\-bios
embeds iron86.
This binary is the standalone smoke tool.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-bios " FILE"
Load IBM 5150 8K BIOS (FE000, reset FFFF:0000).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-fast\-post
Cold POST (do not set BDA RESET_FLAG=1234h).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-audio
Disable PC speaker BEL (default on).
.TP
.B \-\-mda
MDA 80×25 (DIP 0x3D). Default CGA.
.TP
.BI \-\-floppy\-a " PATH"
Drive 0: raw image or host directory packed as FlopFS
(360K if it fits, else 720K 80/2/9).
.TP
.BI \-\-floppy\-b " PATH"
Drive 1: same rules.
.TP
.BI \-\-floppy " PATH"
Alias for
.BR \-\-floppy\-a .
.TP
.BI \-\-keys " STRING"
Type STRING as INT 16h keys.
.TP
.BI \-\-exec\-map " FILE"
1 MiB executed-opcode map.
.SH FLOPPY GEOMETRY
Directory pack is non-recursive, max 32 8.3 names, 360K or 720K only.
Raw images smaller than 300000 bytes use 8 spt / 1 head;
larger use 9 spt / 2 heads (360K and 720K).
1.2M and 1.44M are not auto-detected.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (or guest halt).
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error.
.TP
.B 2
Bad command line.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tdx (1),
.BR tdxview (1)
